## 📱 Native‑app notes (Android / iOS)

If you are building a **mobile app** instead of a web page, the flow is the same conceptually:

| Platform | Key steps |
|----------|-----------|
| **Android** | 1. Add the **Maps SDK for Android** dependency (`implementation 'com.google.android.gms:play-services-maps:18.0.2'`).<br>2. Add the **Location Services** dependency (`implementation 'com.google.android.gms:play-services-location:21.0.1'`).<br>3. Put the API key in `AndroidManifest.xml` (`<meta-data android:name="com.google.android.geo.API_KEY" …>`).<br>4. Request runtime location permission (`ACCESS_FINE_LOCATION`).<br>5. Use `FusedLocationProviderClient` to get the last known location, then call `googleMap.moveCamera(CameraUpdateFactory.newLatLngZoom(...))` and `googleMap.addMarker(new MarkerOptions().position(...))`. |
